| C4 | A3 | REVISED | 1 | `ACCEPTED` | The pre-mission checkpoint shows the last 5 engagements whenever a PM 
selects a country in Create Mission, and success is measured by 60% of new missions having history viewed. The
'last 5' are purely recency-ordered, so routine low-value logs (scheduling emails) can push out the one 
important engagement. With no signal of significance or of how stale the latest entry is, PMs learn to skim 
past the panel. Also, the panel fires before the PM has any assignment to the country or mission. Selecting a 
country in the dropdown should not display engagement summaries for countries the PM does not work on. The 
panel needs the same access filter as C1 and a 'last engagement was N months ago' cue so it conveys useful 
information. |

